From a9ba6f1c60768a22760fce2f674fbfd161f5402f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): the low-light settings next to the IR threshold,
 and Test shows the light

The settings know anti_spoofing.low_light_luma (default 70, 0 = off)
and recognition.ir_low_light_threshold (default 0.7), with the helper's
defaults in defaults.yaml; a config without them loads the defaults,
and a save writes and keeps them (as every other value).

The Thresholds block gets a second row: "Low light below" (the colour
face's brightness, 0-255, a whole-number slider; 0: off) and "IR camera
in low light" (its threshold; it shows when the IR camera's own,
higher threshold applies instead, as the helper never goes below it),
each marked as used or not in the mode (rgb: only with faces enrolled
for the IR camera), with a short explanation and the values measured on
the ASUS Vivobook S 15 (an evening room about 48, daylight 86). An
effective low-light threshold below 0.6 warns as the others do.
Threshold takes a max (above 1 it shows a whole number).

Test reads the helper's light line ("Low light on the colour camera |
face luma 48 < 70: the IR camera decides alone (threshold 0.70)",
"Enough light ...") into its summary: the brightness against the limit
and whether the IR camera decided alone, and at what threshold; the
light lines and "Recognised on the IR camera alone" are in its steps.
Tests: scan (light lines), config (load and save), faceMode.test.ts.
